            <div xml:id="d642">

                <pb facs="0701" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/46: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-18T13:00:00+08:00">March 18, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 18—2:52 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>352. Following from American Consul General, Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 17, 3 p.m. T. Komai,
                            civilian adviser to the Kuantung Army headquarters with the rank of
                            Lieutenant General, has been appointed Director of the General Affairs
                            Department in State Affairs Council <pb facs="0702" n="598"
                                xml:id="pg598"/> of which Premier is the head. A press report from
                            Harbin states that he will become a citizen of the new state.</p>
                        <p>Another report states that C.
                                Ohashi, Japanese Consul General, has been appointed
                            Director of the General Affairs Department in the Ministry of Foreign
                            Affairs. He has just returned from Tokyo.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
